note('charasis/player','blocked_conflicting_classic_key_contract','Howling Stones dungeon-key progression','world_encounter','The complete source adds Hand of Glory17274 master-key/keyring access for six wing doors, then restores exact wing keys after2seconds. P99 positively describes temporary per-wing keys and linear North/West/South/East progression or lockpicking; the entrance Key to Charasis is a different quest. Do not count this imported permanent master-key bypass as a confirmed P99 quest dependency. Current keyring/mutable-door limitations are real but secondary to the unresolved classic key contract. Do not invent a force-open bypass. Separate Ranger1.5 item62637/62638 branches are positively later-era. No missing-page exclusion is used.',[evidence('changes/p99-conversion-world/evidence/charasis-p99-key-review.json','https://wiki.project1999.com/Howling_Stones',note='Research note with source URL, not a copied-page hash.'),base,events])
note('lfaydark/Kalayia_Woodwhisper','blocked_missing_authored_classic_route','Kalayia quest-associated roaming','world_encounter','Perl calls plugin RandomRoam(500,500) repeatedly. Complete plugin requires GetSpawnPoint/GetGuardPoint, authoritative FindGroundZ and CheckLoSToLoc before MoveTo. Those reads/roambox execution are not supplied by current bridge; simply randomizing XY or forcing a straight MoveTo would omit its collision/height safeguards. More importantly P99 specifies a fixed7-8minute route, while local placement76541 has pathgrid0 and no reviewed route coordinates. Current finite-grid support cannot manufacture a classic route from that absence. Vial of Tunare\'s Breath is quest loot, but this entire source is movement-only and neither grants the item nor gates a hand-in. Its absent roaming Lua does not by itself block acquisition or Summoning of Fright progression; this is an ambient route-parity limitation.',[wiki('Kalayia Woodwhisper'),evidence('sources/projecteq/plugins/path_tools.pl'),base,grid])
note('mischiefplane/#Bristlebane','blocked_conflicting_classic_encounter','Bristlebane theater encounter','world_encounter','Full source activates puppet HP waves at80/50/20 and assigns player hate to each. P99 positively describes Bristlebane (God) as an audience/theater appearance produced by Geb, with72-second despawn unless engaged, not these waves. Source claims1.0 but that label alone does not resolve the mismatch. The existing type126160 placement is conditional; no authenticated mapping of the HP-wave puppets to the documented classic appearance is supplied. Do not silently drop HP waves or port a potentially different encounter under this identity.',[wiki('Bristlebane (God)'),spells,public])
